title: Drill — join the wrapped bullet
chapter: 24
type: drill
skills: ex-join
par: 12
minutes: 3
reps: 8
vscode: End, Delete, Space, End, Delete, Space
open: NOTES.md

@brief
Eight times: the bullet on line 4 has been wrapped onto lines 5 and 6.
Make it one line. Do not move the cursor.

@keys
| `:4,6j` | join lines 4 to 6 into one |

@hints
Range, then `j`. Plain `j`, not `j!`: the continuation lines are
indented and you want that indent gone and a space in its place.
--
`:4,6j` and Enter, `:wq`.

@solution
    :4,6j<Enter>  :wq<Enter>

Ten keystrokes. `4G3J` is eight, and `4G` is a jump you then have to jump
back from. This is a drill in reading the gutter and typing the numbers
without thinking about it, because the next three lessons all depend on
that being cheap.

@start NOTES.md
# Sprint notes

- Refund window shipped to staging
- Duplicate charge fix is blocked on
  the gateway team confirming the
  idempotency key format
- Customer tiers in review

@expected NOTES.md
# Sprint notes

- Refund window shipped to staging
- Duplicate charge fix is blocked on the gateway team confirming the idempotency key format
- Customer tiers in review
